[{'by': 'seanccox', 'score': None, 'time': 1387538129, 'title': None, 'type': 'comment', 'url': None, 'text': 'A quick scan of jigneshg&#x27;s past comments reveals that they are definitely not a native English speaker, and as was pointed out above, in Indian culture, this is a perfectly polite way to empathize with another&#x27;s suffering. The irony that this apparent cultural misunderstanding has caused jigneshg&#x27;s karma  to plummet gives me no end of mirth, but the clearly anglophile Western (and perhaps white male) reaction to jigneshg&#x27;s statement is no more accurate for it. There&#x27;s plenty of self-righteous indignation to go around this holiday season, so maybe a little forgiveness is in order, after examining the situation?', 'parent': 6940662, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 6940894, 'ranking': None}, {'by': 'Fuxy', 'score': None, 'time': 1387546409, 'title': None, 'type': 'comment', 'url': None, 'text': 'Interesting.<p>I would like to meet this person.<p>I find it very helpful to surround myself with people that have a different way of seeing the world.', 'parent': 6941171, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 6941271, 'ranking': None}, {'by': 'clhodapp', 'score': None, 'time': 1389167692, 'title': None, 'type': 'comment', 'url': None, 'text': 'They also finally cashed in the &#x27;big side vs. small side&#x27; credit they&#x27;ve been holding onto since they first branded HD (720 and 1080 are the (exact) pixel-lengths of the small sides, while 4k is (less than) the length of the big side).<p>Edit: Not only that, but they can (defendably) make the claim that 4k is &quot;4 times the size of 1080p&quot; while (deniably) knowing that some people will misinterpret.', 'parent': 7022109, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 7022303, 'ranking': None}, {'by': 'MaysonL', 'score': None, 'time': 1340407221, 'title': None, 'type': 'comment', 'url': None, 'text': '"It appears that your web browser does not support webGL", which is bs. They seem to be pushing Chrome, for some reason.', 'parent': 4149250, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 4149396, 'ranking': None}, {'by': 'mhd', 'score': None, 'time': 1367505857, 'title': None, 'type': 'comment', 'url': None, 'text': 'So close, with minimal effort they could map that to \'/bgb/1353\'. It seems that dejure.org actually works that way -&#62; <a href="http://dejure.org/gesetze/BGB/1353" rel="nofollow">http://dejure.org/gesetze/BGB/1353</a> seems to map to <a href="http://dejure.org/gesetze/BGB/1353.html" rel="nofollow">http://dejure.org/gesetze/BGB/1353.html</a>, but they graciously ignore any kind of file extension...', 'parent': 5644486, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 5644753, 'ranking': None}]

