[{'by': 'mulmen', 'score': None, 'time': 1503546477, 'timestamp': 1503546477000000, 'title': '', 'type': 'comment', 'url': '', 'text': 'Yeah good point. In general something like that could still work though.  Whatever characteristics of a page Google is trying to &quot;fix&quot; with AMP could just be added to the ranking algorithm.', 'parent': 15087321, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 15087446, 'ranking': None, 'month': '2017-08-01', 'tags': '[]', 'level': 6, 'post_id': 15085159}, {'by': 'ucaetano', 'score': None, 'time': 1503588429, 'timestamp': 1503588429000000, 'title': '', 'type': 'comment', 'url': '', 'text': '&gt; Where would you draw the line… what percentage of users would have to dislike amp for you to think it was reasonable to add an option?<p>One easy piece of math is (cost of adding and maintaining that feature) vs. [(users who dislike) x (% of users who would quit you) x (profit per user)]<p>For example, if 10% of all users disliked it (300M users), but only 1% of those would leave your services (3M users) and you made, on average, $10 per user in profit, you&#x27;d be putting $30M&#x2F;year of profit at risk, which is probably enough to hire a few people to build and maintain that feature.', 'parent': 15087353, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 15090863, 'ranking': None, 'month': '2017-08-01', 'tags': '[]', 'level': 6, 'post_id': 15085159}, {'by': 'JoshMnem', 'score': None, 'time': 1503580516, 'timestamp': 1503580516000000, 'title': '', 'type': 'comment', 'url': '', 'text': 'It&#x27;s at the expense of the publishers and the future of the open WWW though.', 'parent': 15086941, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 15089791, 'ranking': None, 'month': '2017-08-01', 'tags': '[]', 'level': 6, 'post_id': 15085159}, {'by': 'ucaetano', 'score': None, 'time': 1503537478, 'timestamp': 1503537478000000, 'title': '', 'type': 'comment', 'url': '', 'text': '&gt; The post is critical and frank but well within the bounds of civil discourse.<p>Yeah, this is <i>really</i> within the bounds of &quot;civil discourse&quot;:<p>&gt; Consider doing something more useful with your talents.', 'parent': 15086772, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 15086865, 'ranking': None, 'month': '2017-08-01', 'tags': '[]', 'level': 6, 'post_id': 15085159}, {'by': 'zimpenfish', 'score': None, 'time': 1503571355, 'timestamp': 1503571355000000, 'title': '', 'type': 'comment', 'url': '', 'text': '&gt; It&#x27;s an influential audience<p>I know HN loves to think they&#x27;re influential but I&#x27;d suggest than less than two handfuls of HN users actually have measurable influence outside of HN.', 'parent': 15088216, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'descendants': None, 'id': 15088985, 'ranking': None, 'month': '2017-08-01', 'tags': '[]', 'level': 6, 'post_id': 15085159}]

