[{'id': 1057886, 'by': 'mortenjorck', 'author': 'mortenjorck', 'time': 1263694664, 'time_ts': 1263694664000000, 'text': "Unfortunately, the market is no better. The governments allow their central banks to print fake money while the market allows its financial institutions to print fake assets.<p>Whether it's currencies or CDOs, a bubble is a bubble. Valuation is an art that got lost somewhere in the science.", 'parent': 1057265, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'ranking': 1}, {'id': 3288980, 'by': 'mountaineer', 'author': 'mountaineer', 'time': 1322539234, 'time_ts': 1322539234000000, 'text': 'I\'m sure any investor, including PG, would prefer entrepreneurs to work smarter though, it\'s not just about hours, but it may take that to succeed.<p>But, after reading this, I remembered this PG essay from a few years ago.<p>"Economically, you can think of a startup as a way to compress your whole working life into a few years. Instead of working at a low intensity for forty years, you work as hard as you possibly can for four." - <a href="http://paulgraham.com/wealth.html" rel="nofollow">http://paulgraham.com/wealth.html</a><p>Also:\n<a href="http://paulgraham.com/really.html" rel="nofollow">http://paulgraham.com/really.html</a>', 'parent': 3288867, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'ranking': 1}, {'id': 5318569, 'by': 'mrsebastian', 'author': 'mrsebastian', 'time': 1362410447, 'time_ts': 1362410447000000, 'text': "It's usually pretty quick/easy to get stuff approved for in-lab, early human trials. But yeah, much longer until it's available to the public.", 'parent': 5318538, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'ranking': 1}, {'id': 10281657, 'by': 'mrsteveman1', 'author': 'mrsteveman1', 'time': 1443229031, 'time_ts': 1443229031000000, 'text': 'Sounds a bit like gpg-agent.<p>Do you have plans to support OpenPGPCard devices directly?', 'parent': 10281610, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'ranking': 1}, {'id': 6944241, 'by': 'mschuster91', 'author': 'mschuster91', 'time': 1387575773, 'time_ts': 1387575773000000, 'text': 'Yeah, but the &quot;HF&quot; part of &quot;HFT&quot; tends to make an elephant out of a fly.', 'parent': 6941193, 'deleted': None, 'dead': None, 'ranking': 1}]

